{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520008-non-garou-on-a-pack","id":1520008,"title":"Non Garou on a Pack?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-06T20:03:09-07:00","id":1520008,"title":"Non Garou on a Pack?","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> As per the thread title, can non-garou count as part of the Pack? The Hengeyokai Beast Courts can share a totem, so at least Fera can be part of a pack, but some creatures with similar mechanics to a totem (Nushi for Kuei-Jin) or not so similar but modifiable enough (Totem for shamanic Mages) seem likely to be able to join.<br /> <br /> So, who can join a pack, and what is it needed for that?<br /> <br /> Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T22:35:09-07:00","id":1520016,"title":"","content":"I think as long as you can have the Totem background AND that the spirit in question will accept you as their child (big question), then you could potentially be a pack member as a non-Garou at least mechanically. <br /> <br /> Although I would accept an ST ruling that the Rite of the Totem just does not work on non-Garou, and therefore the non-Garou could never join a pack. The non-Garou might potentially still be the &quot;child&quot; of that spirit, but still not part of the pack that has that spirit as a totem. The pack might view that non-Garou as some kind of bastard stepchild who isn't part of that family. And it brings up a bigger question whether such pack totem spirits would even make themselves available to non-Garou, of if other spirits (even if of the same type) would be sent to non-Garou. A lot depends on how the ST chooses to interpret the setting.<br /> <br /> Whether you can find any Garou who want to be in a pack with you is a bigger question. Garou tend to be very suspicious of any non-Garou, and non-Garou are often physically weaker than Garou, meaning they are not as dependable in a fight. Non-Garou have their own values, and these can often be in conflict with Garou values. There is a big difference between accepting somebody as an ally or friend, and wanting them to be a family member, which is what a pack is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T22:38:21-07:00","id":1520017,"title":"","content":"I think you are mixing up a similar set of mechanics with how things actually work in rhe world. Rituals are ancient pacts with spirits that do a specific thing. The specific thing for the Garou is giving them a higher link to the umbra, bond them as family and coordinate them as a battle group. This is a facet of who Gaia expected them to be. And by default only Garou can be in a Garou pack and their rites only account for Garou.<br /> <br /> Most other shifters do not operate in packs and do not have Totems. As such they don't practice this, except for the Rokea and the Nagah. Even those actually have their own variant rites thar bond them in a way that reasonates with their nature.<br /> <br /> Now these beings were all made for a greater purpose and there are unique and different rites that have been discovered and developed to create either temporary or long term groups of shifters such as kgmandi and the sentai. These rites are highly specific to the spirit pacts made by those societies.<br /> <br /> This means that most Feea cannot be in a pack together without jumping through special hoops. Nothing else can be in a &quot;pack&quot; that doesn't sheir their spirit nature and purpose.<br /> <br /> A hybrid monstrosity of different creatures is not the goal of what a pack should be in Werewolf.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now you can ignore this and just go to Forsaken and lift its rules for hybrid splat packs, but you are going cross to the themes of Werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T23:26:58-07:00","id":1520020,"title":"","content":"Ultimately, it depends how much you're willing to allow custom material from power-sets that are meant to be capable of custom content.<br /> <br /> For example, there is in theory, not Rite that a mage couldn't duplicate, but the books don't really provide much advice for how to accomplish this (esp for things like binding a pack).<br /> <br /> As we've seen with the Beast Courts and the Ahadi, Rites can be created to allow mixed-Fera groups. There's a Rite for a limited quasi-pack to include Kinfolk. There are Rites and Gifts for temporarily including outside Garou into a pack as well. So, clearly, a Rite could be devised or &quot;discovered&quot; for that expand a pack beyond Garou.<br /> <br /> So, within the metaphysics presented so far in the game, it is theoretically possible. Keeping it to the setting as describing, it should be an exceedingly difficult effort to figure out how, but the difficulty of enacting such an effort once someone figures it out is a large unknown. Basically, there's the sliver of the potential in the games to do something, but the default is the potential has never fully been discovered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T09:01:24-07:00","id":1520039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520008-non-garou-on-a-pack?p=1520020#post1520020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately, it depends how much you're willing to allow custom material from power-sets that are meant to be capable of custom content.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>^This. In the rules, it's not possible and I think Kinfolk: Unsung Heroes cover this topic. BUT, the WoD has a plenthora of NPCs which are not possible by the rules. If you want this in your chronicle, if this help in the story, but mainly, if this will be fun in you table... so, go on! Maybe a spirit totem allow the pack and his kinfolk this &quot;gift&quot;, maybe the supernatural rules are broken, maybe this a thing always possible, but none tryed yet or maybe just... happens. It's supernatural rule.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10047-vis\u00e3o-de-\u00e1guia","name":"Vis\u00e3o-de-\u00c1guia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10047_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T12:05:32-07:00","id":1520050,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s contradiction in the rules Kinfolk implies no, whilst Hengeyokai says it\u2019s possible with other Fera and includes the sidebar ruling of a Garou pack master extending his/her Stepping Sideways to Bastet, Mokole (before the latter reach Rank 4) etc <br /> <br /> So even within the rules it\u2019s open to interpretation, plus you thematic examples that you could use such as Pure One Garou sharing a totem with Nunnehi or Hengeyokai Fera sharing a Nushi with the Hungry Dead or Dreamspeaker kinfolk with Garou.<br /> <br /> Theres enough precedents for it to be permissible depending on the background of those involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T15:06:06-07:00","id":1520060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520008-non-garou-on-a-pack?p=1520050#post1520050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There\u2019s contradiction in the rules Kinfolk implies noc</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinfolk require a separate Rite that essentially adds them to the pack as auxillaries. It's in Revised GW and is how the Dies Ultimae operate.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}